femto patch for iri-string 0.7.15
Subject: template: keep the triplets held when the value stops continuing them

Requires 0002.

When the decoder holds the beginning of a character or of a triplet and the
next write does not continue it (`%C3` followed by `x`), push_encoded()
consumes nothing, moves what it held to the output buffer and reports it as
undecodable. DecomposeWriter::write_str() took "nothing consumed" to mean
"nothing to output", flushed the already empty decoder, and went on with the
plain text, so the held triplets were lost: `{+v}` with `%C3%C3x` expanded to
`%C3x`. With a stray `%` at the end of one write and `%` at the start of the
next, the plain text before the next `%` is empty, which a debug assertion
rejected.

Output the result of every push, also when nothing was consumed, and accept
an empty plain prefix.

femto requires a search URL to carry the typed keyword unchanged; a value that
loses bytes on the way is a different search.

